
There are several ways you can implement this method.  This is one way to do it.



Declare two variables, reverse and original, both initialized with the given number.

Initialize reverse to 0. This variable will store the reversed digits of the number.

Use a while loop that continues until the original becomes 0.

Inside the loop:

Multiply reverse by 10 and add the last digit of original (found using original % 10).

Update original by removing its last digit (using original /= 10).

After the loop, compare reverse with the original number. If they are equal, the number is a palindrome.